    "title": "Leveling the playing field for American entrepreneurs",
    "text": "As a former athlete, I learned that competition requires preparation, discipline, and resilience. Those lessons have carried with me throughout my career in business and public service—and they are lessons small-business owners live every day.\nAcross the Mid-Atlantic, entrepreneurs compete for customers, contracts, capital, talent, and new markets. Too often, however, capable small businesses miss opportunities not because they lack a strong product or service, but because they lack access to the right information, relationships, or decision-makers.",
